p_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":458,"cache_read_input_tokens":29037,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":458,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"894da34c-e272-4d7b-b28c-ea90b13b2291","uuid":"5bbc85e0-d3db-46e2-a1c2-aab9050bf387"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":172665,"duration_api_ms":167905,"ttft_ms":3267,"num_turns":27,"result":"All 6 integration tests pass. Summary of what was done:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Configuration analysis:** The `Cargo.toml` had no `[features]` section, so only a single default configuration to verify. The C `CMakeLists.txt` builds a single `libdriver.so` with no conditional compilation flags.\n\n**Issues found and fixed in the Rust translation:**\n\n1. **Missing `#[no_mangle]` exports.** The C `libdriver.so` exports `bad`, `good`, `printLine`, and `printHexCharLine` (in addition to `driver`). The Rust translation only exported `driver`. I converted `print_line`, `print_hex_char_line`, `bad`, and `good` from private Rust fns into `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub extern \"C\" fn` symbols using their C-style names.\n\n2. **`printLine` signature.** Now takes `*const c_char` (matching C's `const char *`) and reads the C string with `CStr::from_ptr`, writing bytes directly to stdout (matching `printf(\"%s\\n\", line)`).\n\n3. **`printHexCharLine` signature.** Now takes `c_char` so external callers can use it via FFI exactly as the C version.\n\n4. **Internal callers updated** to use the C-compatible signatures (passing `*const c_char` for messages, etc.).\n\n**Tests added** (`tests/ffi_parity.rs`):\n- Loads both `c_src/build/libdriver.so` and `target/release/libdriver.so` with `libloading`.\n- Captures stdout via `dup`/`dup2` (so writes from C `printf` are captured too) and asserts byte-for-byte equality.\n- Covers `printLine` (null + several strings), `printHexCharLine` (all 256 i8 values), `bad`, `good`, and `driver` with several inputs.\n\n**Final symbol check:** All user-defined symbols (`bad`, `driver`, `good`, `printHexCharLine`, `printLine`) match between the two `.so` files. (`_init`/`_fini` are linker-generated and not user code.)\n\n**All 6 tests pass.**","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"894da34c-e272-4d7b